== Notes ==
* Though the Runestone's information about them described Necks as lizard-like creatures, they also resembled frogs due to the presence of lily pads on their bodies and their proclivity for hanging around marshy pond areas. The latter alludes to their mythological counterpart's nature as humanoid, shapeshifting water spirits.
*Necks are typically found near shorelines. Especially during rainy weather, necks may be present further inland. 
*They seem to be capable of eating planted crops, such as onions. Beware when growing things where necks can spawn!

== Lore ==
{{Quote|Blue-eyed shufflers in muck, the neck are small lizards native to Valheim. Surly and mean-spirited, they will attack on sight and must be destroyed like vermin. They stay near water because the creatures of the land loathe and abhor them. 
Yet no creature is all bad. Their tails are delicious.|[[Runestone]]}}

The runestone's hostility toward Necks is racially motivated. It does not object to any individual Neck; it condemns the species as a whole, saying that Necks "must be destroyed like vermin" and that "the creatures of the land loathe and abhor them".<ref>In-game text, Meadows runestone (<code>$lore_meadows_random07</code>).</ref>

